<header><h1>The Unofficially Official FAQ and Errata (PoK v3.1.1): Notes</h1></header>
<article>
<p>Every note on this site that <a href="https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_93kw7KkzvAXoQAxRioxo7iAt-Ar6BMIxdNf4Lv25rI/edit" target="_blank" rel="noopener">The Unofficially Official FAQ and Errata (PoK v3.1.1)</a> supports, with the text it is quoted for, grouped by page. <b>Explicit</b> sources state the note directly. <b>Implicit</b> sources support it without stating it.</p>
<h2><a href="/R_abilities">Abilities</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>All abilities that occur &ldquo;after&rdquo; an event occurs all trigger before any abilities that occur &ldquo;before&rdquo; the next event occurs.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling, &ldquo;is &ldquo;after x&rdquo; distinct from &ldquo;before y&rdquo;&rdquo;: &ldquo;They are distinct. &ldquo;After x&rdquo; happens before &ldquo;before y&rdquo;&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A player may resolve &ldquo;at the start of your turn&rdquo; and &ldquo;at the end of your turn&rdquo; abilities on the turn that they pass.<sup>1,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Can you resolve end of turn abilities on the turn you pass? A: Yes.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/R_action_cards">Action Cards</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>Action cards are discarded faceup. Players may look through the action card discard pile.<sup>2,4,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;the discard is public knowledge.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/R_action_phase">Action Phase</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>A player may resolve &ldquo;at the start of your turn&rdquo; and &ldquo;at the end of your turn&rdquo; abilities on the turn that they pass.<sup>1,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Can you resolve end of turn abilities on the turn you pass? A: Yes.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/R_agenda_card">Agenda Card</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>During the agenda phase, if the outcome of an agenda affects multiple players, it does so in speaker order, starting with the speaker and proceeding clockwise. If an agenda is resolved during the action phase, such as with the <a href="/F_keleres">Keleres</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Council_Keleres#Thunder's_Edge_2:~:text=Executive%20Order"><i>Executive Order</i></a> technology, it does so in initiative order.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling (Xxcha hero resolving agendas during the action phase): &ldquo;Initiative order determines the winner. Initiative order is always the lowest initiative player onwards, regardless of who the active player is.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/R_agenda_phase">Agenda Phase</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>During the agenda phase, if the outcome of an agenda affects multiple players, it does so in speaker order, starting with the speaker and proceeding clockwise. If an agenda is resolved during the action phase, such as with the <a href="/F_keleres">Keleres</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Council_Keleres#Thunder's_Edge_2:~:text=Executive%20Order"><i>Executive Order</i></a> technology, it does so in initiative order.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling (Xxcha hero resolving agendas during the action phase): &ldquo;Initiative order determines the winner. Initiative order is always the lowest initiative player onwards, regardless of who the active player is.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/R_anomalies">Anomalies</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>A system containing a <a href="/F_vuilraith">Vuil&rsquo;raith</a> <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Vuil&#x27;Raith_Cabal#:~:text=Dimensional%20Tear">Dimensional Tear</a> is an anomaly.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Are systems that contain Vuil&rsquo;raith Cabal&rsquo;s Dimensional Tears anomalies? A: Yes, any game effect that references an anomaly includes systems containing Dimensional Tears.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The movement restrictions of anomalies are intended to apply to all units, not only ships.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Any units moving into, through or out of anomalies must follow the same rules for ships moving into, through or out of anomalies. This includes units being moved by Mahact&rsquo;s Benediction or moving ground forces with G&rsquo;hom Sek&rsquo;kus.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/R_asteroid_field">Asteroid Field</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>The movement restrictions of anomalies are intended to apply to all units, not only ships.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Any units moving into, through or out of anomalies must follow the same rules for ships moving into, through or out of anomalies. This includes units being moved by Mahact&rsquo;s Benediction or moving ground forces with G&rsquo;hom Sek&rsquo;kus.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/R_attacker">Attacker</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>When the <a href="/F_mahact">Mahact</a> player resolves their <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Mahact_Gene-Sorcerers#Leaders:~:text=Benediction"><i>Benediction</i></a> hero ability, the player that had their ships moved will be the attacker.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;When the Mahact hero, Benediction, is used who is considered the attacker and who is the defender? &hellip; A: The ships being moved belong to the &lsquo;attacker&rsquo; and the ships not being moved belong to the &lsquo;defender.&rsquo;&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/R_bombardment">Bombardment (Unit Ability)</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>Only the active player may bombard.<sup>1,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;only the active player can use BOMBARDMENT.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/R_capture">Capture</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>If a player is eliminated, any of their units that are captured remain with the player that captured them. When the capturing player would return them, the units are instead returned to the game box.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;What happens to captured units when the owner is eliminated? A: Captured units remain on the sheet of the player that captured them. If they would ever be returned to the eliminated player, they are returned to the game box instead.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/R_coexistence">Coexistence</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>Structure limits apply to each player separately. A planet in coexistence may contain up to two PDS and one space dock belonging to each player.<sup>1,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;63.3 does not prevent Titans from placing a PDS on a planet that contains 2 of another player&rsquo;s PDS units. You cannot place a structure on a planet with the maximum number of your structures &hellip;&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/R_combat">Combat (Attribute)</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>Abilities that trigger &ldquo;at the start of a combat&rdquo;, other than those on agents, can only be resolved during a combat in which the player resolving them is participating.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Can abilities that trigger &lsquo;at the start of a combat&rsquo; be played in combats you are not participating in? A: No, any non-agent &lsquo;at the start of a combat&rsquo; abilities must be played during a combat you are participating in.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/R_component_limitations">Component Limitations</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>If a player removes a unit in order to place it, because they have none of that unit type in their reinforcements, that unit is placed undamaged.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If it is produced, placed, or replaced which would require a remove and place it is no longer damaged.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If a player is instructed to &ldquo;replace&rdquo; one unit with another, and they have none of the replacement unit type in their reinforcements, they may remove a unit of that type from any system that does not contain one of their command tokens and place that unit instead.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Any instance of &lsquo;replace&rsquo; can be considered to say &lsquo;remove and place&rsquo; if no units are left in reinforcements, and would be covered by Component Limitations in the LRR.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/R_defender">Defender</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>When the <a href="/F_mahact">Mahact</a> player resolves their <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Mahact_Gene-Sorcerers#Leaders:~:text=Benediction"><i>Benediction</i></a> hero ability, the player that had their ships already in the system will be the defender.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;When the Mahact hero, Benediction, is used who is considered the attacker and who is the defender? &hellip; A: The ships being moved belong to the &lsquo;attacker&rsquo; and the ships not being moved belong to the &lsquo;defender.&rsquo;&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/R_destroyed">Destroyed</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>If a player has a fighter token or infantry token that is not accompanied by a plastic piece of the same type and cannot replace it, the token is removed instead of destroyed.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;When you exceed the number of plastic infantry/fighters available, are unaccompanied tokens removed or destroyed? A: Removed.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/R_elimination">Elimination</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>If an eliminated player had any relic fragments, they are discarded. If an eliminated player had any relics, they are purged.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;What happens to your relics and relic fragments when you&rsquo;re eliminated? A: Relics are purged, relic fragments discarded.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If a player is eliminated, any of their units that are captured remain with the player that captured them. When the capturing player would return them, the units are instead returned to the game box.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Captured units remain on the sheet of the player that captured them. If they would ever be returned to the eliminated player, they are returned to the game box instead.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/R_exploration">Exploration</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>A player may perform transactions after revealing an exploration card and before resolving it.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Can a transaction be performed in the middle of an exploration? A: Yes, transactions may occur after an exploration card is revealed, before the effect is resolved.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If a player is to gain multiple planets in a system, they choose the order in which they gain them, and explore each planet as they gain it before gaining the next.<sup>4,8</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;you choose an order to gain and explore planets. The sequence would be &gt; gain control of planet A &gt; explore planet A &gt; gain control of planet B.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/R_fighter_tokens">Fighter Tokens</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>Unaccompanied fighter tokens are intended to be removed, instead of destroyed.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;When you exceed the number of plastic infantry/fighters available, are unaccompanied tokens removed or destroyed? A: Removed.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/R_game_board">Game Board</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>If the edge of a system tile is touching a hyperlane tile, that edge does not cause that system tile to be on the edge of the game board.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;In maps utilizing hyperlanes (e.g. 5p map), what counts as the edge of the game board? A: Intention is that one of the edges of a system tile does not touch another system tile OR hyperlane tile in order to be considered on the edge of the board.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/R_gravity_rift">Gravity Rift</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>A system containing a <a href="/F_vuilraith">Vuil&rsquo;raith</a> <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Vuil&#x27;Raith_Cabal#:~:text=Dimensional%20Tear">Dimensional Tear</a> is an anomaly.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Are systems that contain Vuil&rsquo;raith Cabal&rsquo;s Dimensional Tears anomalies? A: Yes.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The movement restrictions of anomalies are intended to apply to all units, not only ships.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Any units moving into, through or out of anomalies must follow the same rules for ships moving into, through or out of anomalies. This includes units being moved by Mahact&rsquo;s Benediction or moving ground forces with G&rsquo;hom Sek&rsquo;kus.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/R_ground_combat">Ground Combat</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>Abilities that trigger &ldquo;at the start of a combat&rdquo;, other than those on agents, can only be resolved during a combat in which the player resolving them is participating.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Can abilities that trigger &lsquo;at the start of a combat&rsquo; be played in combats you are not participating in? A: No, any non-agent &lsquo;at the start of a combat&rsquo; abilities must be played during a combat you are participating in.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/R_hyperlanes">Hyperlanes</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>If the edge of a system tile is touching a hyperlane tile, that edge does not cause that system tile to be on the edge of the game board.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Intention is that one of the edges of a system tile does not touch another system tile OR hyperlane tile in order to be considered on the edge of the board.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/R_infantry_tokens">Infantry Tokens</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>If a player has an infantry token that is not accompanied by a plastic infantry and cannot replace it, the token is removed instead of destroyed.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;When you exceed the number of plastic infantry/fighters available, are unaccompanied tokens removed or destroyed? A: Removed.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/R_legendary_planets">Legendary Planets</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>If an effect instructs a player to &ldquo;end your turn&rdquo;, that player may still resolve any &ldquo;at the end of your turn&rdquo; abilities, including those of legendary planets.<sup>4,6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;End of turn abilities can still be used.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/R_movement">Movement</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>When an ability moves a player&rsquo;s ships outside of a tactical action, those ships may transport units out of systems that contain that player&rsquo;s command tokens; this restriction only applies during tactical actions.<sup>1,2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;The LRR will be updated to reflect that transportation of units out of systems that contain your command tokens are only applicable during tactical actions. During Movement abilities, you can transport units out of systems that contain your tokens.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Ships only move &ldquo;into&rdquo; the destination system. A ship may move &ldquo;through&rdquo; other systems.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;When ships move, do they move &lsquo;into&rsquo; systems other than the destination system? A: Only the destination system is considered moved &lsquo;into,&rsquo; other systems are moved &lsquo;through.&rsquo;&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/R_nebula">Nebula</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>The movement restrictions of anomalies are intended to apply to all units, not only ships.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Any units moving into, through or out of anomalies must follow the same rules for ships moving into, through or out of anomalies. This includes units being moved by Mahact&rsquo;s Benediction or moving ground forces with G&rsquo;hom Sek&rsquo;kus.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Units are intended to be able to move into a nebula even when it is not the active system, but not through it.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Nebula rules will be changed. A Nebula will no longer require being the active system in order to move into it. 59.1 will effectively be changed to &lsquo;Units may not move through a Nebula&rsquo;&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Ships can retreat into a nebula, as a nebula is intended to no longer need to be the active system for units to move into it.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Nebula rules will be changed. A Nebula will no longer require being the active system in order to move into it.&rdquo; A retreat moves ships into an adjacent system that is not the active system.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The <a href="/F_saar">Saar</a> player&rsquo;s agent, <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Clan_of_Saar#Leaders:~:text=Captain%20Mendosa">Captain Mendosa</a>, is treated as a bonus and overrides the nebula&rsquo;s move value of 1.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;When leaving a Nebula, is Clan of Saar&rsquo;s agent, Mendosa, applied as a bonus or setting the move value? A: &hellip; Mendosa would be treated as a bonus and would override the Nebula&rsquo;s movement value rule.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/R_objective_cards">Objective Cards</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>A player with three scored secret objectives may draw a fourth. However, they must immediately shuffle it into the secret objective deck.<sup>1,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling, on the scored-secret limit: &ldquo;you could draw an additional secret but would then need to return it and shuffle the secret objective deck.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/R_producing_units">Producing Units</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>If a player removes a unit in order to place it, because they have none of that unit type in their reinforcements, that unit is placed undamaged.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If it is produced, placed, or replaced which would require a remove and place it is no longer damaged.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/R_production">Production (Unit Ability)</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>A player cannot produce ground forces on a planet that contains another player&rsquo;s ground forces.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;You can&rsquo;t produce ground forces on a planet with another player&rsquo;s ground forces.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/R_relics">Relics</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>If the relic deck is empty, a player may still purge relic fragments; they do not gain a relic.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Can a player &lsquo;gain&rsquo; a relic by purging fragments if there are no relics left? A: Yes you can purge relic fragments and not gain a relic if there are none left in the deck.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If an eliminated player had any relic fragments, they are discarded. If an eliminated player had any relics, they are purged.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;What happens to your relics and relic fragments when you&rsquo;re eliminated? A: Relics are purged, relic fragments discarded.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/R_space_combat">Space Combat</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>Abilities that trigger &ldquo;at the start of a combat&rdquo;, other than those on agents, can only be resolved during a combat in which the player resolving them is participating.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Can abilities that trigger &lsquo;at the start of a combat&rsquo; be played in combats you are not participating in? A: No, any non-agent &lsquo;at the start of a combat&rsquo; abilities must be played during a combat you are participating in.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Ships can retreat into a nebula, as a nebula is intended to no longer need to be the active system for units to move into it.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Nebula rules will be changed. A Nebula will no longer require being the active system in order to move into it.&rdquo; A retreat moves ships into an adjacent system that is not the active system.</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/R_supernova">Supernova</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>The movement restrictions of anomalies are intended to apply to all units, not only ships.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Any units moving into, through or out of anomalies must follow the same rules for ships moving into, through or out of anomalies. This includes units being moved by Mahact&rsquo;s Benediction or moving ground forces with G&rsquo;hom Sek&rsquo;kus.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/R_sustain_damage">Sustain Damage</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>A unit may only use its <sc>Sustain Damage</sc> ability once in each timing window, even if it is repaired.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;the same unit could not use its Sustain Damage ability multiple times during the same timing window.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/R_tactical_action">Tactical Action</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>An ability that ends a player&rsquo;s turn ends that turn as soon as it is resolved. No further abilities may be resolved during that same timing window. &ldquo;End of turn&rdquo; abilities may still be resolved.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Any ability that ends your turn should be treated as ending your turn when they occur, and no further abilities during that same trigger window can take place.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling, on the Mahact commander Il Na Viroset: &ldquo;End of turn abilities can still be used.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/R_technology">Technology</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>If a player is instructed to research a technology by any game effect, that player must meet the prerequisites for the technology they research.<sup>1,2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If an ability instructs you to &lsquo;research&rsquo; a technology, you require the prerequisites on that technology to do so.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If a player is instructed to gain a technology, that player does not have to meet the prerequisites.<sup>1,2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If you are instructed to &lsquo;gain&rsquo; or &lsquo;replace&rsquo; a technology, you do not require prerequisites.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/R_transactions">Transactions</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>The Nomad player&rsquo;s <i>Temporal Command Suite</i> technology may allow a second transaction with the same player in one turn.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Does Nomad&rsquo;s Temporal Command Suite faction technology bypass transaction limits? A: Yes, Temporal Command Suite&rsquo;s transaction does not affect performing a second transaction with the same player that turn.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/R_transport">Transport</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>A player&rsquo;s ships are intended to be able to transport units from systems that contain that player&rsquo;s command token when those ships move outside of a tactical action.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;The LRR will be updated to reflect that transportation of units out of systems that contain your command tokens are only applicable during tactical actions. During Movement abilities, you can transport units out of systems that contain your tokens.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/R_victory_points">Victory Points</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>During the action phase, if multiple players gain victory points at the same time, they gain them in initiative order, starting with the player who has the lowest initiative number, regardless of who the active player is.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If the Xxcha hero gives two players in the lead a Victory Point, and both players now have enough points to win the game, is the order for winning determined from Xxcha player (active player) onwards in initiative, or starting with the lowest initiatve? A: Initiative order determines the winner. Initiative order is always the lowest initiative player onwards, regardless of who the active player is.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/R_wormholes">Wormholes</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>A player chooses the path of adjacent systems each ship moves through during movement.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;When you move between systems that both contain a viable wormhole path, you can choose to use those wormholes, a different set of wormholes that are adjacent, or regular adjacency. The player moving the ships chooses the path their ships move through.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the two systems are adjacent because of a wormhole and because of a shared edge or another reason, the player may choose whether or not the ship moves through the wormhole.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;When you move between systems that both contain a viable wormhole path, you can choose to use those wormholes, a different set of wormholes that are adjacent, or regular adjacency. The player moving the ships chooses the path their ships move through.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the two systems are adjacent because of two types of wormholes, the player chooses which type of wormhole the ship moves through.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;When you move between systems that both contain a viable wormhole path, you can choose to use those wormholes, a different set of wormholes that are adjacent, or regular adjacency. The player moving the ships chooses the path their ships move through.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/F_arborec">The Arborec</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>If the player wishes to place a ship, but there are none of that type left in their reinforcements, they may remove a ship of that type from any system that does not contain one of their command tokens and place that instead. This ship will be placed undamaged.<sup>1,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If a unit is damaged, and is &lsquo;removed and placed&rsquo; from the board via a game effect, does it come back repaired &hellip;? A: &hellip; If it is produced, placed, or replaced which would require a remove and place it is no longer damaged.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Arborec player wishes to place a unit, but there are none of that type left in their reinforcements, they may remove a unit of that type from any system that does not contain one of their command tokens and place that instead. This unit will be placed undamaged.<sup>1,3,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If a unit is damaged, and is &lsquo;removed and placed&rsquo; from the board via a game effect, does it come back repaired &hellip;? A: &hellip; If it is produced, placed, or replaced which would require a remove and place it is no longer damaged.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/F_argent">The Argent Flight</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li><sc>Raid Formation</sc> occurs when hits are produced, not after hits are assigned. As such, canceling any hits will not prevent an opponent&rsquo;s ships from becoming damaged.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;When is Raid Formation applied? After rolling or after assigning hits? &hellip; A: Raid formation is applied after rolling, before cancelling or assigning hits.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The chosen ship becomes damaged, it does not use its <sc>Sustain Damage</sc> ability. As such, effects that trigger when a ship uses its <sc>Sustain Damage</sc> ability, such as the <i>Direct Hit</i> action card, cannot be played.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Can ships damaged by Raid Formation trigger a window for the Direct Hit Action card? A: No, Raid Formation does not cause the ship to use its Sustain Damage ability, it only causes it to become damaged.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>When a Strike Wing Alpha II rolls a 9 or 10 for their <sc>anti&ndash;fighter barrage</sc> ability, infantry are destroyed before any hits are canceled.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Does Strike Wing Alpha II infantry killing get prevented by Shields Holding/re-roll abilities? A: &hellip; the infantry would be destroyed BEFORE any cancellation of hits.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Effects that cancel hits, such as the <i>Shields Holding</i> action card, cannot prevent the infantry from being destroyed. If an effect rerolls any anti&ndash;fighter barrage dice, the new result will determine how many infantry are destroyed.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;The rolls from Strike Wing Alpha II can be subject to rerolls before the ability is applied, but the infantry would be destroyed BEFORE any cancellation of hits.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Ships may transport units out of systems that contain one of the Argent player&rsquo;s command tokens.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;During Movement abilities, you can transport units out of systems that contain your tokens.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Ships moved with <i>Helix Protocol</i> must still follow the rules for moving into anomalies, such as supernovas.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Unofficially Official FAQ, Anomalies: &ldquo;Any units moving into, through or out of anomalies must follow the same rules for ships moving into, through or out of anomalies.&rdquo; (names Benediction and G&rsquo;hom Sek&rsquo;kus, not Helix Protocol)</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/F_letnev">The Barony of Letnev</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li><sc>Munitions Reserves</sc> may only be used to reroll combat rolls. It cannot be used to reroll anti&ndash;fighter barrage rolls and similar.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Can War Funding Omega be used on Anti-Fighter Barrage rolls? A: No, War Funding Omega, War Funding, Munitions Reserves and Crown of Thalnos, are specific to combat rolls.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A player may only reroll combat rolls with <i>War Funding</i>. They cannot reroll anti&ndash;fighter barrage rolls and similar.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Can War Funding Omega be used on Anti-Fighter Barrage rolls? A: No, War Funding Omega, War Funding, Munitions Reserves and Crown of Thalnos, are specific to combat rolls.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A player may only reroll combat rolls with <i>War Funding &Omega;</i>. They cannot reroll anti&ndash;fighter barrage rolls and similar.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Can War Funding Omega be used on Anti-Fighter Barrage rolls? A: No, War Funding Omega, War Funding, Munitions Reserves and Crown of Thalnos, are specific to combat rolls.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>This ability only applies to combat rolls. It does not apply to dice rolls for a unit&rsquo;s <sc>Anti&ndash;Fighter Barrage</sc> ability.<sup>1,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Does the Barony of Letnev agent, Viscount Unlenn, allow an extra dice to be rolled during AFB? A: No, the Barony agent only has an effect on combat rolls.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/F_saar">The Clan of Saar</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>The effect of Captain Mendosa occurs when the system is activated.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;How does Clan of Saar&rsquo;s agent, Mendosa, interact with abilities that increase movement such as Gravity Drive or Flank Speed? A: Clan of Saar&rsquo;s agent, Mendosa, will get an errata to &lsquo;WHEN you activate a system.&rsquo; This means other bonuses would be applied after Mendosa takes effect.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Move value modifying effects that trigger after a system is activated, such as the <i>Flank Speed</i> action card or the <i>Gravity Drive</i> technology will not be included in Captain Mendosa&rsquo;s effect.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;How does Clan of Saar&rsquo;s agent, Mendosa, interact with abilities that increase movement such as Gravity Drive or Flank Speed? A: Clan of Saar&rsquo;s agent, Mendosa, will get an errata to &lsquo;WHEN you activate a system.&rsquo; This means other bonuses would be applied after Mendosa takes effect.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Gravity rifts apply the +1 during movement. This modifier will not be included in Captain Mendosa&rsquo;s effect.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;How does Clan of Saar&rsquo;s agent, Mendosa, interact with abilities that increase movement such as Gravity Drive or Flank Speed? A: Clan of Saar&rsquo;s agent, Mendosa, will get an errata to &lsquo;WHEN you activate a system.&rsquo; This means other bonuses would be applied after Mendosa takes effect.&rdquo; A gravity rift&rsquo;s +1 is applied during movement, after Mendosa takes effect.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The nebula effect of setting the move value of all ships in that system to one will be overwritten by Captain Mendosa&rsquo;s effect.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;When leaving a Nebula, is Clan of Saar&rsquo;s agent, Mendosa, applied as a bonus or setting the move value? A: &hellip; Mendosa would be treated as a bonus and would override the Nebula&rsquo;s movement value rule.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/F_keleres">Council Keleres</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>The Keleres player chooses their starting technology after all other players have gained their starting technologies.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;What is the order of gaining starting technology when Winnu and/or Argent Flight are in a game with Council Keleres? &hellip; A: Keleres selects after all other players have selected their starting technology.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If there is only one unique starting technology among those owned by other players, the Keleres player will start the game with only one technology.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Keleres only gets one starting technology if there is only one other starting technology among all other factions at the table.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If this ability is used, all laws are blanked. The Keleres player cannot choose for some laws to remain in effect.<sup>4,12</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;How does the Council Keleres faction ability Law&rsquo;s Order interact &hellip;? A: All agendas are treated as blank for all players for the duration of that Council Keleres player&rsquo;s turn.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The Keleres player and all of the other players treat all laws as blank for the turn.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;How does the Council Keleres faction ability Law&rsquo;s Order interact &hellip;? A: All agendas are treated as blank for all players for the duration of that Council Keleres player&rsquo;s turn.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The blanked laws come back into effect at the end of the turn.<sup>4,12</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;How does the Council Keleres faction ability Law&rsquo;s Order interact &hellip;? A: All agendas are treated as blank for all players for the duration of that Council Keleres player&rsquo;s turn.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Any abilities that trigger &ldquo;when/after a unit uses <sc>Production</sc>&rdquo; will trigger an additional time, for example, the <i>Sarween Tools</i> technology.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Yes, Sarween Tools would trigger with each instance of PRODUCTION (twice).&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The additional <sc>Production</sc> ability cannot belong to the same unit as the original <sc>Production</sc> ability.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;No, the second PRODUCTION instance must be different than one of the units that used the ability to trigger Agency Supply Network.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>During a tactical action, the active player must use every <sc>Production</sc> ability of their units in the active system, or none of them. As such, the additional <sc>Production</sc> ability must belong to a unit in a different system.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;PRODUCTION is all or nothing during tactical actions, so you couldn&rsquo;t choose to only use one ability in a system to then use another one in the same system.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The Custodia Vigilia planet card is gained exhausted.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Does Custodia Vigilia count as a planet for objectives? Agendas? &hellip;&rdquo; &ldquo;It is gained exhausted.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Units cannot be placed on Custodia Vigilia.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Does Custodia Vigilia count as a planet for objectives? Agendas? &hellip;&rdquo; &ldquo;units cannot be placed on it.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Custodia Vigilia is not on the game board, and does not exist in a system.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Does Custodia Vigilia count as a planet for objectives? Agendas? &hellip;&rdquo; &ldquo;This planet is not on the game board, and does not exist in a system.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The Keleres player cannot be eliminated once they control Custodia Vigilia.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Does Custodia Vigilia count as a planet for objectives? Agendas? &hellip;&rdquo; &ldquo;Keleres cannot be eliminated if they control Custodia Vigilia.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Custodia Vigilia may be used to qualify for objectives, if it meets any other requirements listed.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Does Custodia Vigilia count as a planet for objectives? Agendas? &hellip;&rdquo; &ldquo;It counts as a planet for objectives and agendas if it meets the specific criteria of those objectives and agendas.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The <sc>Production</sc> value that the Custodia Vigilia legendary planet ability gives Mecatol Rex counts toward the <i>Produce en Masse</i> objective.<sup>4,9</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Unofficially Official FAQ: &ldquo;Does Custodia Vigilia&rsquo;s PRODUCTION count as a unit for sarween tools, etc.? A: Yes, Custodia Vigilia should include &ldquo;as if it were a unit&rdquo;.&rdquo; The legendary ability reads: &ldquo;While you control Mecatol Rex, it gains SPACE CANNON 5 and PRODUCTION 3.&rdquo; Produce en Masse counts the combined PRODUCTION value of units in a single system, so Mecatol Rex&rsquo;s PRODUCTION 3 counts.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Custodia Vigilia counts as a planet for agendas if it meets the specific criteria of those agendas.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Does Custodia Vigilia count as a planet for objectives? Agendas? &hellip;&rdquo; &ldquo;It counts as a planet for objectives and agendas if it meets the specific criteria.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Custodia Vigilia only gives command tokens when the Imperial strategy card is used to gain a victory point for controlling Mecatol Rex, not when it is used to score a public objective.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Does Custodia Vigilia give command tokens when a player scores public objectives off Imperial? A: No, the intent is that the tokens are only gained off of using Imperial&rsquo;s ability to gain a Victory Point because you control Mecatol Rex.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>When the Keleres player uses the <sc>Production</sc> ability of Custodia Vigilia, it is treated as though it were a unit.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Does Custodia Vigilia&rsquo;s PRODUCTION count as a unit for sarween tools, etc.? A: Yes, Custodia Vigilia should include &lsquo;as if it were a unit&rsquo;.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>This may trigger the abilities of the <i>Sarween Tools</i> technology, and other similar abilities.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Same ruling: &ldquo;Yes.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The <a href="/F_ul">Ul</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Titans_of_Ul#Faction_Promissory_Note:~:text=Terraform"><i>Terraform</i></a> faction promissory note may be attached to Custodia Vigilia.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Does Custodia Vigilia count as a planet for objectives? Agendas? &hellip;&rdquo; &ldquo;Terraform can be placed on it.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If <i>Terraform</i> is attached to Custodia Vigilia, it may be explored.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Does Custodia Vigilia count as a planet for objectives? Agendas? &hellip;&rdquo; &ldquo;It may be explored.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Xander Alexin Victori III applies to only a single instance of spending trade goods.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;What is the duration of the Council Keleres agent &hellip;? A: The agent is exhausted at the time the commodities would be spent as trade goods, and only lasts for the duration of that spend.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The Keleres player must be participating in the combat in order to resolve <i>Overwing Zeta</i>.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling, General: &ldquo;Can abilities that trigger &ldquo;at the start of a combat&rdquo; be played in combats you are not participating in? A: No, any non-agent &ldquo;at the start of a combat&rdquo; abilities must be played during a combat you are participating in.&rdquo; Overwing Zeta is a hero, not an agent, and triggers at the start of a round of space combat.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If a planet contains multiple mechs, the invading player must pay one influence for each, as separate payments.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;How does the influence payment for the Council Keleres mech, Omniopiares, stack in multiples? Each a separate payment? A: Each mech is one instance of spend one influence.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/F_muaat">The Embers of Muaat</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>If a player already owns their war sun unit upgrade technology, they cannot play <i>Fires of the Gashlai</i>.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Can a player resolve an ability to gain a technology when they already have that technology (Fires of the Gashlai)? A: No, you are not resolving the ability fully if you already have the specified technology.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li><i>Nova Seed</i> purges all tokens on the replaced system tile other than command tokens and frontier tokens. Any faction&ndash;specific tokens, such as <a href="/F_creuss">Creuss</a> wormhole tokens or <a href="/F_ul">Ul</a> sleeper tokens, are returned to the player that owns them instead.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;How does The Embers of Muaat Hero, Nova Seed, interact with tokens &hellip;? A: Nova Seed also purges all tokens other than command tokens and frontier tokens. Any faction specific tokens are returned to that faction.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/F_hacan">The Emirates of Hacan</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>If the Hacan player has their <i>Political Secret</i> played during an agenda, they may still trade action cards, as <sc>Arbiters</sc> is a passive ability.<sup>1,2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Can Hacan trade action cards after having Political Secret played against them? A: Arbiters is a passive ability and the Emirates of Hacan can trade Action cards regardless.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The ability of Carth of Golden Sands cannot be resolved while another ability is resolving. For example, if the Hacan player is exploring an industrial planet and has revealed the card, they cannot use the ability of Carth of Golden Sands until after they resolve the card&rsquo;s effect.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;transactions may occur after an exploration card is revealed, before the effect is resolved, but other abilities may not be used until after the effect is resolved.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The planet cannot be traded during combat.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;A planet that has the Hacan Mech can&rsquo;t be traded in combat.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/F_empyrean">The Empyrean</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>The trade goods gained from <i>Dark Pact</i> are gained simultaneously with the commodities transacted between the two players.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;When a player gives you their commodities and triggers Dark Pact, do you gain all the trade goods simultaneously or the Dark Pact TG separately? &hellip; A: It is a single gain of commodities and 1 TG simultaneously.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>As the trade goods from <i>Dark Pact</i> are gained simultaneously with any commodities and/or trade goods transacted, the <a href="/F_mentak">Mentak</a> player may only use their <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Mentak_Coalition#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Pillage"><sc>Pillage</sc></a> ability on each player once per <i>Dark Pact</i> transaction.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Same ruling, asked &ldquo;(For the purposes of Pillage)&rdquo;: &ldquo;It is a single gain of commodities and 1 TG simultaneously.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A unit may only use its <sc>Sustain Damage</sc> ability once in each timing window, even if it is repaired.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;the same unit could not use its Sustain Damage ability multiple times during the same timing window.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Influence must be spent separately for each use of this ability. As such, any excess influence used to repair a ship is wasted, and cannot be used to repair a different ship.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;The Dynamo&rsquo;s ability can be used multiple times in the same combat round by spending 2 influence, individually, each time.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A system that contains a planet destroyed by the <i>Stellar Converter</i> relic, and no other planets, is considered to contain no planets.<sup>4,6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;The destroyed planet token is no longer a planet for any purpose, and if it is covering the only planet in a system, that system contains no planets.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A system that contains a planet destroyed by the <i>Stellar Converter</i> relic, and no other planets, is considered to contain no planets.<sup>4,6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;The destroyed planet token is no longer a planet for any purpose, and if it is covering the only planet in a system, that system contains no planets.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/F_creuss">The Ghosts of Creuss</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>The fighters are placed one at a time, until either one has been placed for each ship with capacity that moved through a wormhole, or the capacity of the system is reached.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;When Sai Seravus is used, fighters are placed in the active system one at a time, up to the number of ships with capacity that moved through wormholes, or the capacity limit in the system is reached, whichever happens first.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Any tokens on either system are moved with their system.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling, Creuss hero Singularity Reactor and tokens: &ldquo;All tokens stay with their original tile&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/F_lizix">The L1Z1X Mindnet</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>If the L1Z1X player would have to place a structure, but there are none of that type left in their reinforcements, they may, but are not required to, remove a structure of that type from any system that does not contain one of their command tokens and place that instead.<sup>1,2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Any instance of &lsquo;replace&rsquo; can be considered to say &lsquo;remove and place&rsquo; if no units are left in reinforcements, and would be covered by Component Limitations in the LRR.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The L1Z1X player cannot use their <sc>Harrow</sc> ability if they are not the active player.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Can the L1Z1X use harrow when they&rsquo;re defending during ground combat? A: No, only the active player can use BOMBARDMENT.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If a player wishes to place a mech, but there are none left in their reinforcements, they may remove a mech from any system that does not contain one of their command tokens and place that instead. The mech will be placed undamaged.<sup>1,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If a unit is damaged, and is &lsquo;removed and placed&rsquo; from the board via a game effect, does it come back repaired &hellip;? A: &hellip; If it is produced, placed, or replaced which would require a remove and place it is no longer damaged.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>When the L1Z1X player&rsquo;s ships move outside of a tactical action, they may transport units from systems that contain the L1Z1X player&rsquo;s command tokens.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;The LRR will be updated to reflect that transportation of units out of systems that contain your command tokens are only applicable during tactical actions. During Movement abilities, you can transport units out of systems that contain your tokens.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Ships moving out of a gravity rift must roll for removal.<sup>1,2,3,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Do ships roll when moving out of a gravity rift due to the Mahact Hero, Benediction? A: Yes.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/F_mahact">The Mahact Gene&ndash;Sorcerers</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>If an agenda requires the Mahact player to remove one of their command tokens from their fleet pool, and they only have other players&rsquo; command tokens in their fleet pool, they must remove one of those tokens, and return it to the reinforcements of the player that owns it.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If you are the Mahact player, what happens when an agenda tells you to &lsquo;remove one of your command tokens from your fleet pool &hellip;&rsquo; but you only have tokens from&rdquo; other players? &ldquo;A: You are required to remove another player&rsquo;s token and return it to that player&rsquo;s reinforcements.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the <i>Fleet Regulations</i> law limits the number of tokens the Mahact player may have in their fleet pool, they may still add a command token to their fleet pool when they are at the limit, but must then remove one command token and return it to the corresponding reinforcements.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If the law Fleet Regulations is in play, and Mahact already has 4 tokens in fleet, can they add another one &hellip;? A: The Mahact player can add a 5th token and choose one to return to their reinforcements from their fleet pool afterward.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A player that cannot vote due to a game effect or because they have zero influence on readied planets cannot be targeted by <i>Genetic Recombination</i>.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Genetic Recombination happens before a player would exhaust planets to vote. So if a player cannot vote, or does not have votes to cast, they cannot be targeted by the tech.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If a player then gains the ability to vote, they may then be targeted by <i>Genetic Recombination</i>.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If they obtain an ability that would allow them to vote, they could be targeted by the tech before the votes are cast.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The Mahact player cannot use any &ldquo;when/after you activate a system&rdquo; abilities.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;In regards to the Mahact Commander, Il Na Viroset, when does your turn end? &hellip; Is this different from Nullification Field or Starlancer? A: &hellip; when/after you activate and other abilities within your turn cannot be used when the Mahact player places a second token in a system. End of turn abilities can still be used. Any ability that ends your turn should be treated as ending your turn when they occur, and no further abilities during that same trigger window can take place.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Other players cannot use any &ldquo;when/after another player activates a system that&hellip;&rdquo; abilities.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;In regards to the Mahact Commander, Il Na Viroset, when does your turn end? &hellip; Is this different from Nullification Field or Starlancer? A: &hellip; when/after you activate and other abilities within your turn cannot be used when the Mahact player places a second token in a system. End of turn abilities can still be used. Any ability that ends your turn should be treated as ending your turn when they occur, and no further abilities during that same trigger window can take place.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The Mahact player may still use any &ldquo;at the end of your turn&rdquo; abilities.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;In regards to the Mahact Commander, Il Na Viroset, when does your turn end? &hellip; Is this different from Nullification Field or Starlancer? A: &hellip; when/after you activate and other abilities within your turn cannot be used when the Mahact player places a second token in a system. End of turn abilities can still be used. Any ability that ends your turn should be treated as ending your turn when they occur, and no further abilities during that same trigger window can take place.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Mahact player places a second command token in a system using Il Na Viroset, the <i>Counterstroke</i> action card cannot be played.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;What&rsquo;s the interaction with the Mahact Commander, Il Na Viroset, and the Counterstroke action card? A: Counterstroke cannot be played.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Mahact player places a second command token in a system using Il Na Viroset, the <i>Dark Energy Tap</i> technology does not trigger.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Does Dark Energy Tap trigger if you used the Mahact Commander, Il Na Viroset? A: No.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Mahact player moves another player&rsquo;s ships, ground forces on planets are left behind.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;When using the Mahact Hero, Benediction, can the Mahact player transport other players&rsquo; ground forces from planets? Can the units&rsquo; owner transport ground forces from planets? A: No in both circumstances.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Mahact player moves their own ships, they may transport ground forces on planets.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;When using the Mahact Hero, Benediction, can the Mahact player transport their own ground forces from planets when moving? A: Yes.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Mahact player moves a player&rsquo;s ships out of a gravity rift, that player must roll for removal.<sup>3,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Do ships roll when moving out of a gravity rift due to the Mahact Hero, Benediction? A: Yes.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The system the combat is taking place in is considered the active system during that combat.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;The combat system is treated as the active system during that combat.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The player whose ships were moved is considered to be the attacker, the other player is considered to be the defender.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;The ships being moved belong to the &lsquo;attacker&rsquo; and the ships not being moved belong to the &lsquo;defender.&rsquo;&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;When using the Mahact Hero, Benediction, if another player&rsquo;s fleet is moved into a Mahact fleet, who is the attacker/defender? A: The player that is moved is the attacker, the player that is moved into is the defender.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>After the ships are moved, capacity is checked before the space combat begins.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;When using the Mahact Hero, Benediction, is capacity resolved after moving ships before the space combat? &hellip; A: A Capacity check is resolved before the space combat begins.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The Starlancer must be in the system before activation to be able to use its ability.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If Mahact has an Arborec Command Token in their fleet pool &hellip; can the Mahact player produce a mech &hellip;? A: No, the mech was not in the system at the time of activation, so it didn&rsquo;t see the trigger for its ability.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Once the Mahact player resolves the ability of a Starlancer, the active player cannot use any &ldquo;after you activate a system&rdquo; abilities.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;In regards to the Mahact Commander, Il Na Viroset, when does your turn end? &hellip; Is this different from Nullification Field or Starlancer? A: &hellip; when/after you activate and other abilities within your turn cannot be used when the Mahact player places a second token in a system. End of turn abilities can still be used. Any ability that ends your turn should be treated as ending your turn when they occur, and no further abilities during that same trigger window can take place.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Other players, including the Mahact player, cannot use any &ldquo;after another player activates a system that&hellip;&rdquo; abilities.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;In regards to the Mahact Commander, Il Na Viroset, when does your turn end? &hellip; Is this different from Nullification Field or Starlancer? A: &hellip; when/after you activate and other abilities within your turn cannot be used when the Mahact player places a second token in a system. End of turn abilities can still be used. Any ability that ends your turn should be treated as ending your turn when they occur, and no further abilities during that same trigger window can take place.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The active player may still use any &ldquo;at the end of your turn&rdquo; abilities.<sup>4,6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;In regards to the Mahact Commander, Il Na Viroset, when does your turn end? &hellip; Is this different from Nullification Field or Starlancer? A: &hellip; when/after you activate and other abilities within your turn cannot be used when the Mahact player places a second token in a system. End of turn abilities can still be used. Any ability that ends your turn should be treated as ending your turn when they occur, and no further abilities during that same trigger window can take place.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The Mahact player may use the ability to end their own turn and gain their own spent command token from their fleet pool.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling, &ldquo;Can Mahact use their mech ability on themselves?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Can Mahact use their mech ability on themselves? A: Yes.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/F_mentak">The Mentak Coalition</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>If a game effect instructs a player to convert their commodities to trade goods, that player does not gain any trade goods from that effect. The Mentak player cannot use their <sc>Pillage</sc> ability for those trade goods.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;whenever commodities are converted to a player&rsquo;s own trade good area, they are not considered gained.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If all of the Mentak player&rsquo;s ships are destroyed, they may still place ships with this ability. If they do, combat will continue.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If Mentak&rsquo;s Hero, Sleeper Cell, is used and their last ship is destroyed during a round of combat in which they also destroy an opponent&rsquo;s ship, does combat continue? A: Yes.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Both players will choose and destroy one of their own ships in the active system for each hit their opponent produced during each round of combat, before the Mentak player places their ships for the <i>Sleeper Cell</i> ability.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;after both players assign hits the Mentak player then places a ship from their reinforcements in the active system and combat continues.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Mentak player wishes to place a unit with this ability, but there are none of that type left in their reinforcements, they may remove a unit of that type from any system that does not contain one of their command tokens and place that instead. This unit will be placed undamaged.<sup>1,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If a unit is damaged, and is &lsquo;removed and placed&rsquo; from the board via a game effect, does it come back repaired &hellip;? A: &hellip; If it is produced, placed, or replaced which would require a remove and place it is no longer damaged.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Mentak_Coalition#Flagship:~:text=Fourth%20Moon"><i>Fourth Moon</i></a> is destroyed during combat, but the Mentak player then destroys their opponent&rsquo;s flagship and places the <i>Fourth Moon</i> back into the combat, they cannot score the <i>Unveil Flagship</i> objective.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If you use the Mentak Coalition&rsquo;s Hero &hellip; and lose your flagship in a combat, but destroy the other player&rsquo;s flagship and rebuild your own, can you score Unveil Flagship? A: No.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The Mentak player cannot place a war sun unless they have their war sun technology.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Can the Mentak Coalition&rsquo;s hero, Sleeper Cell, be used to place a warsun if you do not own the warsun technology? A: No.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/F_naalu">The Naalu Collective</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>Ships moving out of a gravity rift with <sc>Foresight</sc> must roll for removal.<sup>1,2,3,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Any units moving into, through or out of anomalies must follow the same rules for ships moving into, through or out of anomalies.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The chosen player is considered to be the active player.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;The Naalu Collective agent, Z&rsquo;eu Omega &hellip; effectively makes them the active player for the duration of the tactical action &hellip; This DOES NOT count as the tactical action player&rsquo;s turn, so they cannot utilize fleet logistics, however they could use Master Plan or the Minister of War &hellip; Minister of Peace and the Mahact Gene-Sorcerers mech, Starlancer ends the turn of the tactical action&rdquo; player.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the chosen player is not the Naalu player, it is not considered their turn for game effects.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;The Naalu Collective agent, Z&rsquo;eu Omega &hellip; effectively makes them the active player for the duration of the tactical action &hellip; This DOES NOT count as the tactical action player&rsquo;s turn, so they cannot utilize fleet logistics, however they could use Master Plan or the Minister of War &hellip; Minister of Peace and the Mahact Gene-Sorcerers mech, Starlancer ends the turn of the tactical action&rdquo; player.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the chosen player is not the Naalu player, they cannot use the <i>Fleet Logistics</i> technology to perform an additional action.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;The Naalu Collective agent, Z&rsquo;eu Omega &hellip; effectively makes them the active player for the duration of the tactical action &hellip; This DOES NOT count as the tactical action player&rsquo;s turn, so they cannot utilize fleet logistics, however they could use Master Plan or the Minister of War &hellip; Minister of Peace and the Mahact Gene-Sorcerers mech, Starlancer ends the turn of the tactical action&rdquo; player.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The chosen player may use the <i>Master Plan</i> action card or the <i>Minister of War</i> agenda to perform an additional action.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;The Naalu Collective agent, Z&rsquo;eu Omega &hellip; effectively makes them the active player for the duration of the tactical action &hellip; This DOES NOT count as the tactical action player&rsquo;s turn, so they cannot utilize fleet logistics, however they could use Master Plan or the Minister of War &hellip; Minister of Peace and the Mahact Gene-Sorcerers mech, Starlancer ends the turn of the tactical action&rdquo; player.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The <i>Minister of Peace</i> agenda and the <a href="/F_mahact">Mahact</a> player&rsquo;s Starlancer mech still end the chosen player&rsquo;s tactical action, even though it is not considered their turn.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;The Naalu Collective agent, Z&rsquo;eu Omega &hellip; effectively makes them the active player for the duration of the tactical action &hellip; This DOES NOT count as the tactical action player&rsquo;s turn, so they cannot utilize fleet logistics, however they could use Master Plan or the Minister of War &hellip; Minister of Peace and the Mahact Gene-Sorcerers mech, Starlancer ends the turn of the tactical action&rdquo; player.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The Naalu player may choose to produce one fighter for one resource. If they do, they may produce one additional fighter.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Can the Naalu Collective commander, M&rsquo;aban, or the Yin Brotherhood commander, Brother Omar, allow the player to choose to produce only 1 infantry/fighter and then another with their commander? A: Yes.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The Naalu player cannot look at the agenda deck while a player is resolving the primary ability of the Politics strategy card.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;It also cannot be used to interrupt the primary ability of the Politics strategy card.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>When the <i>Covert Legislation</i> agenda is revealed during the agenda phase, the Naalu player cannot look at the hidden agenda.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;The Naalu Collective Commander, M&rsquo;aban Omega, cannot look at the next card when Covert Legislation is revealed before the speaker draws the top card of the agenda deck.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/F_naaz_rokha">The Naaz&ndash;Rokha Alliance</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>The Naaz&ndash;Rokha player must choose to use this ability before seeing the first exploration card.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;For the Naaz-Rokha&rsquo;s Distant Suns ability, do you decide to draw the extra exploration card before you draw the first card, or after? A: Before the initial exploration card is drawn.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the relic deck is empty, the Naaz&ndash;Rokha player may still purge two relic fragments as an action.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Can a player &lsquo;gain&rsquo; a relic by purging fragments if there are no relics left? A: Yes you can purge relic fragments and not gain a relic if there are none left in the deck.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Naaz&ndash;Rokha player has no command tokens in their reinforcements, they may still purge one relic fragment as an action.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Can you purge a relic fragment to gain a command token if you have no command tokens in your reinforcements? A: Yes, you can purge the fragment and not gain a command token if there are none in reinforcements.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the relic deck is empty, a player may still purge two relic fragments as an action to resolve <i>Black Market Forgery</i>, but they do not gain a relic.<sup>1,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling, &ldquo;Can a player &ldquo;gain&rdquo; a relic by purging fragments if there are no relics left?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Yes you can purge relic fragments and not gain a relic if there are none left in the deck.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Naaz&ndash;Rokha player has no command tokens in their reinforcements, they must use a command token from their command sheet when performing the secondary ability of the strategy cards.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling, Naaz-Rokha hero Hesh and Prit with no tokens in reinforcements: &ldquo;The LRR will be updated to be more general towards taking off sheet if none are in reinforcements.&rdquo; general rule for taking tokens from sheet.</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/F_nekro">The Nekro Virus</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>The Nekro player cannot use <i>The Prophet&rsquo;s Tears</i> relic to draw an action card when they gain a technology using this ability.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;They cannot do this when they GAIN technology via their Technological Singularity faction ability.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Nekro player owns <i>The Prophet&rsquo;s Tears</i> relic, they may draw an action card whenever they would research a technology.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Can the Nekro Virus player use the Prophet&rsquo;s Tears Relic? A: Yes, when the Nekro virus player uses their Propagation faction ability, they could exhaust the Relic to gain an action card.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The player holding <i>Antivirus</i> may only play it at the start of a combat they are participating in.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Can abilities that trigger &lsquo;at the start of a combat&rsquo; be played in combats you are not participating in? A: No, any non-agent &lsquo;at the start of a combat&rsquo; abilities must be played during a combat you are participating in.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the <a href="/F_jol_nar">Jol&ndash;Nar</a> player uses their hero to replace a technology which is currently being copied by a <i>Valefar Assimilator</i>, it will remain copied with a Valefar Assimilator token on it while in that player&rsquo;s technology deck.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;The token stays on the tech in the tech-deck and Valefar Assimilator still has that technology&rsquo;s text.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Ground forces on planets remain there while participating in combat.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Ground Forces participating in space combat via The Alastor do not move from their origin location. If they were on planets at the start of combat, they stay on the planet.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>When the Nekro player is in a space combat against the <a href="/F_argent">Argent</a> player, their infantry on planets participating in the combat cannot be targeted by the ability of the Argent player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Argent_Flight#Destroyer:~:text=Strike%20Wing%20Alpha%20II"><i>Strike Wing Alpha II</i></a> destroyers.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If they were on planets at the start of combat, they stay on the planet, participate in combat, and are immune to SWA2&rsquo;s ability.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The ability of Nekro Malleon cannot be resolved while another ability is resolving.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Can I use the Nekro Virus&rsquo; Agent, Nekro Malleon &hellip; to interrupt another ability since the timing is &lsquo;during the action phase&rsquo;? A: No, any ability that is used &lsquo;during the action phase&rsquo; cannot be resolved unless there are no other abilities currently being resolved.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/F_nomad">The Nomad</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>If the <i>Deadly Plot</i> action card is played, the Nomad will not gain a trade good from <sc>Future Sight</sc>.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;What is the interaction between Deadly Plot and prediction abilities, given that Deadly Plot specifically says &lsquo;resolved with no effect&rsquo;. A: &lsquo;Resolved with no effect&rsquo; is not an outcome that could have been predicted, so no prediction abilities can trigger.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li><i>Temporal Command Suite</i> may allow the Nomad player to perform a second transaction with another player during one turn.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Does Nomad&rsquo;s Temporal Command Suite faction technology bypass transaction limits? A: Yes, Temporal Command Suite&rsquo;s transaction does not affect performing a second transaction with the same player that turn.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Any damaged mechs remain damaged.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If a unit is damaged, and is &lsquo;removed and placed&rsquo; from the board via a game effect, does it come back repaired or does it remain damaged. A: If it is being removed and placed via an ability such as Transit Diodes it stays in the same state.&rdquo; Field Marshal Mercer removes and places ground forces the same way Transit Diodes does.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nomad#Flagship:~:text=Memoria"><i>Memoria</i></a> may transport ground forces from systems containing one of the Nomad player&rsquo;s command tokens while the ability of Ahk&ndash;Syl Siven is active.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Does the Nomad&rsquo;s Hero, Ahk-Syl Siven, allow their flagship to pick up groundforces in systems that contain their tokens? A: Yes.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>During a space combat, a Quantum Manipulator cannot be repaired by the <i>Duranium Armor</i> technology, as it is not participating in the combat.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Does the Duranium Armor technology allow you to repair Nomad Mechs that have used their ability to cancel a hit during space combat? A: No, Duranium Armor only affects units participating (rolling dice) in a combat.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/F_norr">Sardakk N&rsquo;orr</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li><i>Valkyrie Particle Weave</i> produces a hit before any hits may be canceled. Canceling the original hits will not cause the additional hit to be canceled.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Does Valkyrie Particle Weave trigger after hits were produced if the hits were cancelled? A: Yes, the hit from Valkyrie Particle Weave is still applied.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>This ability allows the N&rsquo;orr player to commit ground forces to a planet even if they did not move any ships into the active system.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Can Sardakk N&rsquo;orr&rsquo;s commander, G&rsquo;hom Sek&rsquo;kus, be used without moving any ships into the active system? A: Yes.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The N&rsquo;orr player may only commit ground forces as the active player.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Can the Sardakk N&rsquo;orr player commit ground forces via their commander, G&rsquo;hom Sek&rsquo;kus, on defense? A: No, only the active player can commit ground forces.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The N&rsquo;orr player must legally be able to move into the destination system in order to commit ground forces with G&rsquo;hom Sek&rsquo;kus.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Does a Ceasefire promissory note have any impact on committing ground forces from adjacent planets via Sardakk N&rsquo;orr&rsquo;s commander &hellip;? A: Will change &lsquo;commit ground forces&rsquo; in LRR to say &lsquo;move&rsquo; to ensure Ceasefire works. Will also prevent units from being committed to planets in anomalies without the appropriate technology, or through wormholes if Enforced Travel Ban is a Law.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If another player plays the N&rsquo;orr player&rsquo;s <i>Ceasefire</i> promissory note, they cannot commit any ground forces to planets in the active system during this action, other than ground forces already in the active system.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Does a Ceasefire promissory note have any impact on committing ground forces from adjacent planets via Sardakk N&rsquo;orr&rsquo;s commander &hellip;? A: Will change &lsquo;commit ground forces&rsquo; in LRR to say &lsquo;move&rsquo; to ensure Ceasefire works. Will also prevent units from being committed to planets in anomalies without the appropriate technology, or through wormholes if Enforced Travel Ban is a Law.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The N&rsquo;orr player cannot commit ground forces to planets in an asteroid field, unless the N&rsquo;orr player owns the <i>Antimass Deflectors</i> technology.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Does a Ceasefire promissory note have any impact on committing ground forces from adjacent planets via Sardakk N&rsquo;orr&rsquo;s commander &hellip;? A: Will change &lsquo;commit ground forces&rsquo; in LRR to say &lsquo;move&rsquo; to ensure Ceasefire works. Will also prevent units from being committed to planets in anomalies without the appropriate technology, or through wormholes if Enforced Travel Ban is a Law.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The N&rsquo;orr player cannot commit ground forces through a wormhole if the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Sardakk_N&#x27;orr#:~:text=Enforced%20Travel%20Ban"><i>Enforced Travel Ban</i></a> law is in play.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Does a Ceasefire promissory note have any impact on committing ground forces from adjacent planets via Sardakk N&rsquo;orr&rsquo;s commander &hellip;? A: Will change &lsquo;commit ground forces&rsquo; in LRR to say &lsquo;move&rsquo; to ensure Ceasefire works. Will also prevent units from being committed to planets in anomalies without the appropriate technology, or through wormholes if Enforced Travel Ban is a Law.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Purging the <i>Dominus Orb</i> relic does not allow the N&rsquo;orr player to use G&rsquo;hom Sek&rsquo;kus to commit ground forces from systems that contain their command tokens.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Does using Dominus Orb allow the Sardakk N&rsquo;orr player to commit ground forces via their commander &hellip;? A: No, G&rsquo;hom Sek&rsquo;kus is explicitly preventing committing from systems with tokens, and Dominus Orb is purged several steps before committing takes place.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Only the active player may use the <sc>Bombardment</sc> ability of their units during an invasion.<sup>3,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;only the active player can use BOMBARDMENT.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>This prevents the <a href="/F_lizix">L1Z1X</a> player from using their <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_L1Z1X_Mindnet#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Harrow"><sc>Harrow</sc></a> faction ability, unless they are the active player.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Can the L1Z1X use harrow when they&rsquo;re defending during ground combat? A: No, only the active player can use BOMBARDMENT.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/F_ul">The Titans of Ul</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>The Ul player may place a PDS on a planet that contains two of another player&rsquo;s PDS. They cannot place a PDS on a planet that already contains two of their own PDS.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Does 63.3 (2 PDS on a planet max) mean that Titans couldn&rsquo;t place a PDS via Sleeper token onto a planet where another player already has 2 PDS? &hellip; A: 63.3 does not prevent Titans from placing a PDS on a planet that contains 2 of another player&rsquo;s PDS units. You cannot place a structure on a planet with the maximum number of your structures.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Ul player wishes to place a PDS, but there are none left in their reinforcements, they may remove a PDS from any system that does not contain one of their command tokens and place that instead. The PDS will be placed undamaged.<sup>1,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If a unit is damaged, and is &lsquo;removed and placed&rsquo; from the board via a game effect, does it come back repaired &hellip;? A: &hellip; If it is produced, placed, or replaced which would require a remove and place it is no longer damaged.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Ul player&rsquo;s units exist in the same location as another player&rsquo;s units, effects that end the Ul player&rsquo;s turn cannot prevent the combat from occurring.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If you awaken a sleeper token or deploy your flagship and then your turn ends (Mahact mech, Nullification field, Minister of Peace), do you resolve combat? A: Coalescence forces combat steps to occur.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Only the active player may use the <sc>Bombardment</sc> ability of their units during an invasion.<sup>3,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;only the active player can use BOMBARDMENT.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>This prevents the <a href="/F_lizix">L1Z1X</a> player from using their <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_L1Z1X_Mindnet#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Harrow"><sc>Harrow</sc></a> ability.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Can the L1Z1X use harrow when they&rsquo;re defending during ground combat? A: No, only the active player can use BOMBARDMENT.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Ul player&rsquo;s turn is ended by another game effect, the combat still occurs. No other steps of the tactical action occur, and abilities may only be used within that combat.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Coalescence forces combat steps to occur. No other steps of the tactical action occur, and abilities can only be used within combat.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Once played, <i>Terraform</i> counts as being in the play area of the player who controls the planet.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Yes, when Terraform is attached to a planet it counts as being in that planet owner&rsquo;s play area.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Ul player gains control of a planet with <i>Terraform</i> attached, their own <i>Terraform</i> will be in their play area.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Yes, when Terraform is attached to a planet it counts as being in that planet owner&rsquo;s play area.&rdquo; Applies when the Ul player owns the planet.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Effects that move ground forces, such as the <i>Ghost Squad</i> action card or the ability of the <a href="/F_norr">N&rsquo;orr</a> player&rsquo;s commander, <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Sardakk_N&#x27;orr#:~:text=G%27hom%20Sek%27kus">G&rsquo;hom Sek&rsquo;kus</a>, (via the <i>Alliance</i> promissory note), cannot be used to move a Hel&ndash;Titan to another planet.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Can the Titans Hel-Titan move via abilities like the action card Ghost Squad or via the Sardakk N&rsquo;Orr Alliance? A: No, structures cannot move.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The timing of Tellurian is changed to &ldquo;before you assign a hit&rdquo;, the same as the <i>Shields Holding</i> action card and the <sc>Sustain Damage</sc> ability. As such, if Tellurian cancels a hit produced by a player who owns the <a href="/F_norr">N&rsquo;orr</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Sardakk_N&#x27;orr#:~:text=Valkyrie%20Particle%20Weave"><i>Valkyrie Particle Weave</i></a> technology, <i>Valkyrie Particle Weave</i> still triggers before the hit is canceled.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;The Titan&rsquo;s Agent will receive an errata to have the same timing as Shields Holding or Sustain Damage. &lsquo;Before you assign a hit&rsquo;. The hit is still produced, VPW triggers, then the hit is canceled.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The trade good may be spent on the units produced by the <sc>Production</sc> ability that triggered Tungstantus.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling, Ul commander Tungstantus: &ldquo;The gain and spend are simultaneous, so cannot be pillaged.&rdquo; gain and spend are simultaneous.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The trade good may be spent as it is gained. The number of trade goods the Ul player has after producing units is used to determine if the <a href="/F_mentak">Mentak</a> player may use their <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Mentak_Coalition#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Pillage"><sc>Pillage</sc></a> ability.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling, Ul commander Tungstantus: &ldquo;The gain and spend are simultaneous, so cannot be pillaged.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The Ul player must have at least one PDS in their reinforcements to place in order to use the <sc>Deploy</sc> ability of a Hecatoncheires. However, when they would place a PDS, they may remove a PDS from any system that does not contain one of their command tokens and put it in their reinforcements. They may then use the <sc>Deploy</sc> ability of a Hecatoncheires.<sup>1,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;You also cannot DEPLOY a mech if you have no PDS in reinforcements, but could remove a PDS from the board and then DEPLOY your mech to an eligible target planet.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The Ul player cannot place a PDS on a planet that already has two of their PDS on it. As such, they are unable to place a Hecatoncheires on a planet with two of their PDS using its <sc>Deploy</sc> ability.<sup>3,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Does 63.3 (2 PDS on a planet max) mean that Titans couldn&rsquo;t place a PDS via Sleeper token onto a planet where another player already has 2 PDS? &hellip; A: 63.3 does not prevent Titans from placing a PDS on a planet that contains 2 of another player&rsquo;s PDS units. You cannot place a structure on a planet with the maximum number of your structures.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Same ruling: &ldquo;which prevents using the DEPLOY ability on a planet with 2 PDS of yours.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/F_jol_nar">The Universities of Jol&ndash;Nar</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>All replacements happen simultaneously. If this ability returns a specific technology, it cannot then be regained via this ability.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling, Jol-Nar hero Rin: &ldquo;Simultaneously, that is to say the Universities of Jol-Nar player cannot swap out a tech and re-take it during this component action.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If this ability is used to replace a faction technology which is currently being copied by the Nekro player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Valefar%20Assimilator"><i>Valefar Assimilator</i></a> technology, the Valefar Assimilator token stays on that technology while it is in the technology deck, and <i>Valefar Assimilator</i> still has that technology&rsquo;s text.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If the Universities of Jol-Nar player replaces a faction technology with their hero, what happens if the Nekro Virus player had a Valefar Assimilator token on it? A: The token stays on the tech in the tech-deck and Valefar Assimilator still has that technology&rsquo;s text.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/F_vuilraith">The Vuil&rsquo;raith Cabal</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>When an opponent&rsquo;s Infantry II is destroyed during combat, the Vuil&rsquo;raith player captures an infantry token, and the opponent rolls for resurrection, placing the destroyed infantry on the Infantry II unit upgrade card if successful.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling, &ldquo;What is the interaction between Infantry 2 and Capture?&rdquo;: &ldquo;What is the interaction between Infantry 2 and Capture? A: Both happen&rdquo; both capture and resurrection apply.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Each gravity rift will still provide its usual +1 to each ship&rsquo;s move value.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Can a ship benefit from the Vuil&rsquo;raith Cabal promissory note, The Crucible &hellip;? A: Yes &hellip; the bonus would apply to all ships that can make it to the active system, including the bonuses from the promissory and the rift they are passing through.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If a ship could move from its current system to the active system through a gravity rift if its move value were +2, it may do so using <i>Crucible</i>. This is true even if that ship could not reach the gravity rift without <i>Crucible</i>.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Can a ship benefit from the Vuil&rsquo;raith Cabal promissory note, The Crucible, if it would not be able to reach a gravity rift on the way to the active system without it? A: Yes.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>For example, consider a series of systems X&ndash;S&ndash;G&ndash;Y. Only systems connected by a &ldquo;&ndash;&rdquo; are adjacent. System &ldquo;G&rdquo; is a gravity rift. Systems &ldquo;X&rdquo;, &ldquo;S&rdquo; and &ldquo;Y&rdquo; are standard systems with no movement restrictions. A ship with a move value of one is in system &ldquo;X&rdquo;. Were it to have +2 to its movement value, it could reach system &ldquo;Y&rdquo;. Currently, that ship may reach only system &ldquo;S&rdquo;. Despite this, if its owner activated system &ldquo;Y&rdquo; and played <i>Crucible</i>, the ship could move to that system.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Same ruling: &ldquo;the bonus would apply to all ships that can make it to the active system.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li><i>Vortex</i> cannot be used if there are no units that can be targeted.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling, Vuil&rsquo;raith Vortex: &ldquo;Can Vortex be used on a ship if a player doesn&rsquo;t have any of those ships in their reinforcements? A: No, since they cannot fully resolve Vortex.&rdquo; Vortex cannot be used without a unit it can capture.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If a player has all their units of a particular type on the board, other than fighters or infantry, that type of unit belonging to that player cannot be targeted.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling, Vuil&rsquo;raith Vortex: &ldquo;No, since they cannot fully resolve Vortex.&rdquo; cannot target if none in reinforcements.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A system containing a Dimensional Tear is an anomaly.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Are systems that contain Vuil&rsquo;raith Cabal&rsquo;s Dimensional Tears anomalies? A: Yes, any game effect that references an anomaly includes systems containing Dimensional Tears.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>When <i>The Terror Between</i> is destroyed, it still captures units that were destroyed at the same time.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Does the Cabal Flagship capture other units that are destroyed in the same timing window in which it is destroyed? A: Yes.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If a player loses their commodities immediately after replenishing them, most commonly via that player&rsquo;s <i>Trade Agreement</i> promissory note, the Vuil&rsquo;raith player may still target them. If they do, they still use that player&rsquo;s full commodity value to determine which units may be captured.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Can the Vuil&rsquo;raith Cabal use their agent on someone who has their Trade Agreement used to take their commodities? A: Yes, the commodities would not be there but the agent could still be used to capture a ship up to the player&rsquo;s commodity value.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>When The Stillness of Stars converts a player&rsquo;s commodities to trade goods, those trade goods are not treated as being gained for the purpose of triggering other abilities. In particular, the <a href="/F_mentak">Mentak</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Vuil&#x27;Raith_Cabal#:~:text=Pillage"><sc>Pillage</sc></a> faction ability is not triggered by this ability.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Does Cabal Agent count as &lsquo;converting your own commodities&rsquo; &hellip;? A: No, whenever commodities are converted to a player&rsquo;s own trade good area, they are not considered gained.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Vuil&rsquo;raith player owns the Infantry II unit upgrade technology, and one is destroyed during ground combat on a planet with a Reanimator, the Vuil&rsquo;raith player captures an infantry token, and they roll for resurrection, placing the destroyed infantry on the Infantry II unit upgrade card if successful.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling, &ldquo;What is the interaction between Infantry 2 and Capture?&rdquo;: &ldquo;What is the interaction between Infantry 2 and Capture? A: Both happen&rdquo; both capture and resurrection apply.</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/F_winnu">The Winnu</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>If a system meets two (or more) of the conditions listed, Rickar Rickani will only apply +2 to combat rolls, not +4 (or +6).<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Does the Winnu commander, Rickar Rickani, stack if Mecatol Rex is also a Legendary Planet? A: No, the commander only triggers once no matter how many conditions are met.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/F_xxcha">The Xxcha Kingdom</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>Once the Xxcha player resolves the ability of <i>Nullification Field</i>, the active player cannot use any &ldquo;after you activate a system&rdquo; abilities.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling on Il Na Viroset, which asks &ldquo;Is this different from Nullification Field?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Any ability that ends your turn should be treated as ending your turn when they occur, and no further abilities during that same trigger window can take place.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The active player may still use any &ldquo;at the end of your turn&rdquo; abilities.<sup>4,6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Same ruling: &ldquo;End of turn abilities can still be used.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A planet must be exhausted to be targeted by Ggrocuto Rinn.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Can the Xxcha Agent, Ggrocuto Rinn, be used to &lsquo;ready&rsquo; a planet that is not exhausted? A: The target planet must be exhausted.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Xxcha player draws the <i>Covert Legislation</i> agenda, they will only draw a hidden agenda if they choose to reveal it. If the Xxcha player is not the speaker, the speaker will view the hidden agenda.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Xxcha would only get to see the agenda tied to Covert Legislation if it was one of the 2 agendas selected to resolve and they are the speaker, otherwise the speaker would see the agenda.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>When the Xxcha player chooses and reveals an agenda, they may then use their <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Xxcha_Kingdom#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Quash"><sc>Quash</sc></a> ability.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Can the Xxcha Kingdom player play riders while using their hero &hellip;? A: Yes, the Xxcha player can play riders, and use their quash ability during their hero &hellip; Other players cannot play any action cards as these are abilities.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>After the Xxcha player chooses and reveals an agenda, they may play any rider action cards on the revealed agenda.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Can the Xxcha Kingdom player play riders while using their hero &hellip;? A: Yes, the Xxcha player can play riders, and use their quash ability during their hero &hellip; Other players cannot play any action cards as these are abilities.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>When an agenda outcome with an immediate effect resolves, all players resolve the effect.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling, Xxcha hero Xxekir Grom and agendas: &ldquo;The intent is that players still resolve agendas that the Xxcha player chooses off of their Hero.&rdquo; all players resolve agenda effects.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If an agenda would give multiple players a victory point, those players gain that victory point in initiative order, regardless of the Xxcha player&rsquo;s initiative.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If the Xxcha hero gives two players in the lead a Victory Point &hellip; A: Initiative order determines the winner.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The effect of the <i>Checks and Balances</i> agenda that occurs &ldquo;at the end of this agenda phase&rdquo; is ignored.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Checks and balances against reads &lsquo;Each player readies only 3 of their planets at the end of this agenda phase.&rsquo; Does this trigger at the end of Xxchas hero? &hellip; A: This effect does not trigger if it happens during the Xxcha Hero.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Other players cannot play action cards, including riders, while the Xxcha player resolves <i>Political Data Nexus</i>.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Can the Xxcha Kingdom player play riders while using their hero &hellip;? A: Yes, the Xxcha player can play riders, and use their quash ability during their hero &hellip; Other players cannot play any action cards as these are abilities.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Xxcha player draws an agenda that is replaced if there are no laws in play, and there are no laws in play, a new agenda is drawn.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If there are no laws in play a new agenda is drawn.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>During the status phase, public and secret objectives are scored simultaneously. The Xxcha player cannot score a public objective, unlock Xxekir Grom, and then use <i>Political Data Nexus &Omega;</i> in order to score a secret objective, or vice versa.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Scoring in the status phase is done all at once, the unlock condition of heroes is not checked until the score objectives step of the status phase is complete.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The combined value may be spent as either influence or resources, not both.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;When using an ability that references &lsquo;resource value&rsquo;, the printed resource value of the planet is used.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li><i>Political Data Nexus &Omega;</i> does not change the value used by abilities that reference a planet&rsquo;s resource value; the printed resource value of the planet is used.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If the Xxcha Kingdom plays uprising with Political Data Nexus Omega unlocked do they get the sum &hellip;? A: When using an ability that references &lsquo;resource value&rsquo;, the printed resource value of the planet is used.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/F_yin">The Yin Brotherhood</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>If all of a player&rsquo;s ships are destroyed during combat, they may still place ships with this ability. If they do, combat will continue.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Does the Yin Brotherhood agent, Brother Milor, keep combat going after the last ship is destroyed? A: Yes.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling, on a similar effect, the Mentak hero: &ldquo;after both players assign hits the Mentak player then places a ship &hellip; and combat continues.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If all ships in the system are destroyed by hits produced from a space cannon roll, the player that produced those hits may score the <i>Turn Their Fleets to Dust</i> secret objective before the new fighters are placed.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If the last ship in a system is destroyed, TTFTD could be scored for destroying the last ship, then after the Yin agent would trigger.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Brother Milor &Omega; may only be used during the action phase.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Can the Yin Brotherhood Agent, Brother Milor Omega, be used during the Agenda Phase? A: Brother Milor Omega can only be used during the action phase.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If all of a player&rsquo;s units in a combat are destroyed, they may still place units with this ability. If they do, combat will continue.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling, on the earlier Brother Milor: &ldquo;Does the Yin Brotherhood agent, Brother Milor, keep combat going after the last ship is destroyed? A: Yes.&rdquo; The Ω card places units the same way.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If all ships in the system are destroyed by hits produced from a space cannon roll, the player that produced those hits may score the <i>Turn Their Fleets to Dust</i> secret objective before the new fighters are placed.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If the last ship in a system is destroyed, TTFTD could be scored for destroying the last ship, then after the Yin agent would trigger.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Yin player uses Brother Milor &Omega; when a unit is destroyed that is both a ground force and a ship due to some game effect, that unit&rsquo;s owner may place two fighters or two infantry.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;The units participating in combat via these flagship abilities are both a ground force and ship during combat. The owner of the unit can choose whether to place 2 infantry or 2 fighters when using Brother Milor Omega, however units placed this way can only continue to participate in space combat if fighters are placed, and can only continue to participate in ground combat if infantry are placed.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If placed this way during a space combat, any newly placed infantry cannot participate. If placed this way during a ground combat, any newly placed fighters cannot participate.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;The units participating in combat via these flagship abilities are both a ground force and ship during combat. The owner of the unit can choose whether to place 2 infantry or 2 fighters when using Brother Milor Omega, however units placed this way can only continue to participate in space combat if fighters are placed, and can only continue to participate in ground combat if infantry are placed.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If all of a player&rsquo;s units in a combat are destroyed, they may still place units with this ability. If they do, combat will continue.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling, on the earlier Brother Milor: &ldquo;Does the Yin Brotherhood agent, Brother Milor, keep combat going after the last ship is destroyed? A: Yes.&rdquo; The ΩΩ card places units the same way.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Yin player uses Brother Milor &Omega;&Omega; when a unit is destroyed that is both a ground force and a ship due to some game effect, that unit&rsquo;s owner may place two fighters or two infantry.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;The units participating in combat via these flagship abilities are both a ground force and ship during combat. The owner of the unit can choose whether to place 2 infantry or 2 fighters when using Brother Milor Omega, however units placed this way can only continue to participate in space combat if fighters are placed, and can only continue to participate in ground combat if infantry are placed.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If placed this way during a space combat, any newly placed infantry cannot participate. If placed this way during a ground combat, any newly placed fighters cannot participate.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;The units participating in combat via these flagship abilities are both a ground force and ship during combat. The owner of the unit can choose whether to place 2 infantry or 2 fighters when using Brother Milor Omega, however units placed this way can only continue to participate in space combat if fighters are placed, and can only continue to participate in ground combat if infantry are placed.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The Yin player may choose to produce one infantry for one resource. If they do, they may produce one additional infantry.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Can the Naalu Collective commander, M&rsquo;aban, or the Yin Brotherhood commander, Brother Omar, allow the player to choose to produce only 1 infantry/fighter and then another with their commander? A: Yes.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>As such, each time the Yin player spends one resource on infantry, they may produce one, two or three infantry.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;both of these commanders allow the player to choose to only build a single fighter/infantry for 1 resource and gain an additional unit of that type each time they do.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Only the <b>Commit Ground Forces</b>, <b>Ground Combat</b> and <b>Establish Control</b> steps of an invasion are resolved on the chosen planets; the <b>Bombardment</b> and <b>Space Cannon Defense</b> steps are not.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;The Yin hero, Quantum Dissemination Omega, should indicate to resolve ground combats on those planets, not full invasion steps. Parley can be played on one of the planets.&rdquo; The question it answers asks about &ldquo;committing additional ground forces, and using bombardment&rdquo;; committing the 3 infantry and establishing control over planets won are implied by the card text.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The <i>Parley</i> action card may be used on one planet when the Yin player resolves <i>Quantum Dissemination</i>.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;The Yin hero, Quantum Dissemination Omega, should indicate to resolve ground combats on those planets, not full invasion steps. Parley can be played on one of the planets.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/C_action_cards">Action Cards</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li><i>Confounding Legal Text</i> is played before revealing the hidden agenda for the <i>Covert Legislation</i> agenda, and before the <i>Drive the Debate</i> objective may be scored.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;&rsquo;Legal Text&rsquo; ACs would be played before Drive the Debate can be scored.&rdquo; And: &ldquo;The &lsquo;Legal Text&rsquo; action cards and Deadly Plot must be played before the agenda that was voted on is revealed.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li><i>Confusing Legal Text</i> is played before revealing the hidden agenda for the <i>Covert Legislation</i> agenda, and before the <i>Drive the Debate</i> objective may be scored.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;&rsquo;Legal Text&rsquo; ACs would be played before Drive the Debate can be scored.&rdquo; And: &ldquo;The &lsquo;Legal Text&rsquo; action cards and Deadly Plot must be played before the agenda that was voted on is revealed.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The active player may still use any &ldquo;at the end of your turn&rdquo; abilities.<sup>4,6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;In regards to the Mahact Commander, Il Na Viroset, when does your turn end? &hellip; Is this different from Nullification Field or Starlancer? A: &hellip; when/after you activate and other abilities within your turn cannot be used when the Mahact player places a second token in a system. End of turn abilities can still be used. Any ability that ends your turn should be treated as ending your turn when they occur, and no further abilities during that same trigger window can take place.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Any prediction made for a rider or similar ability is incorrect, and will not resolve.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;&rsquo;Resolved with no effect&rsquo; is not an outcome that could have been predicted, so no prediction abilities can trigger.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A player cannot make the prediction that <i>Deadly Plot</i> will be played when they predict the outcome of an agenda.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;&rsquo;Resolved with no effect&rsquo; is not an outcome that could have been predicted, so no prediction abilities can trigger.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li><i>Deadly Plot</i> is played before revealing the hidden agenda for the <i>Covert Legislation</i> agenda.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;The &lsquo;Legal Text&rsquo; action cards and Deadly Plot must be played before the agenda that was voted on is revealed.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If a mech is damaged when it is removed, it will remain damaged when it is placed.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If it is being removed and placed via an ability such as Transit Diodes it stays in the same state.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A player must still meet the prerequisites for the technology they research.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If an ability instructs you to &lsquo;research&rsquo; a technology, you require the prerequisites on that technology to do so.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A player must still meet the prerequisites for the technology they research.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If an ability instructs you to &lsquo;research&rsquo; a technology, you require the prerequisites on that technology to do so.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The <a href="/F_ul">Ul</a> player cannot use <i>Ghost Squad</i> to move a Hel&ndash;Titan.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Q: Can the Titans Hel-Titan move via abilities like the action card Ghost Squad &hellip;? A: No, structures cannot move.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If a player has scored three secret objectives, they may use <i>Impersonation</i> to draw a secret objective, then immediately shuffle it into the secret objective deck.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Q: Can you resolve the Impersonation action card to draw a secret objective if you are already at your limit of scored secret objectives? A: Yes, you could draw an additional secret but would then need to return it and shuffle the secret objective deck.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If a player wishes to place a structure, but there are none of that type left in their reinforcements, they may remove a structure of that type from any system that does not contain one of their command tokens and place that instead. That player may make the choice for each structure.<sup>1,2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;You also cannot DEPLOY a mech if you have no PDS in reinforcements, but could remove a PDS from the board and then DEPLOY your mech.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The <a href="/F_ul">Ul</a> player will place each of their Hel Titan PDS undamaged.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling, damaged unit removed and placed: &ldquo;If it is produced, placed, or replaced which would require a remove and place it is no longer damaged.&rdquo; a placed unit is undamaged.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A player does not need to meet the prerequisites of the technology they gain from <i>Plagiarize</i>.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If you are instructed to &lsquo;gain&rsquo; or &lsquo;replace&rsquo; a technology, you do not require prerequisites.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If a player has no mechs left in their reinforcements, they may remove a mech from any system that does not contain one of their command tokens and place that instead. The mech will be placed undamaged.<sup>1,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If a unit is damaged, and is &lsquo;removed and placed&rsquo; from the board via a game effect, does it come back repaired &hellip;? A: &hellip; If it is produced, placed, or replaced which would require a remove and place it is no longer damaged.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If <i>Reflective Shielding</i> is played after a ship uses its <sc>Sustain Damage</sc> ability during an <b>Assign Hits</b> step, then the hits produced by <i>Reflective Shielding</i> are added to any other hits produced in the immediately preceding <b>Roll Dice</b> step.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Q: When are the hits generated by reflective shielding assigned? A: &hellip; If during the normal assign hits step, they are added to the pool of hits already generated.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If <i>Reflective Shielding</i> is played after a ship uses its <sc>Sustain Damage</sc> ability at any other time during combat, the hits are assigned immediately.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;The hits are immediately assigned if not during the normal assign hits step.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A player must still meet the prerequisites for the technology they research.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If an ability instructs you to &lsquo;research&rsquo; a technology, you require the prerequisites on that technology to do so.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>It is public knowledge which action cards a player takes using <i>Reverse Engineer</i>.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling, on The Codex relic: &ldquo;the discard is public knowledge, so anything removed from the discard is also public knowledge.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A player must still meet the prerequisites for the technology they research.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If an ability instructs you to &lsquo;research&rsquo; a technology, you require the prerequisites on that technology to do so.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If a player wishes to place a dreadnought, but there are none left in their reinforcements, they may remove a dreadnought from any system that does not contain one of their command tokens and place that instead. This dreadnought will be placed undamaged.<sup>1,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If a unit is damaged, and is &lsquo;removed and placed&rsquo; from the board via a game effect, does it come back repaired &hellip;? A: &hellip; If it is produced, placed, or replaced which would require a remove and place it is no longer damaged.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If a player wishes to place a cruiser, but there are none left in their reinforcements, they may remove a cruiser from any system that does not contain one of their command tokens and place that instead. This cruiser will be placed undamaged.<sup>1,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If a unit is damaged, and is &lsquo;removed and placed&rsquo; from the board via a game effect, does it come back repaired &hellip;? A: &hellip; If it is produced, placed, or replaced which would require a remove and place it is no longer damaged.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If a player wishes to place a dreadnought, but there are none left in their reinforcements, they may remove a dreadnought from any system that does not contain one of their command tokens and place that instead. This dreadnought will be placed undamaged.<sup>1,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If a unit is damaged, and is &lsquo;removed and placed&rsquo; from the board via a game effect, does it come back repaired &hellip;? A: &hellip; If it is produced, placed, or replaced which would require a remove and place it is no longer damaged.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/C_agendas">Agendas</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>A player with three scored secret objectives may draw a fourth. However, they must immediately shuffle it into the secret objective deck.<sup>1,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling, on Impersonation at the scored-secret limit: &ldquo;you could draw an additional secret but would then need to return it and shuffle the secret objective deck.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the speaker draws an agenda that would be replaced when it is revealed, such as <i>Miscount Disclosed</i>, they follow the text of that agenda and draw a new agenda.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If Covert Legislation draws an agenda that self-replaces (e.g. miscount disclosed), does it replace immediately? A: Follow the text, draw a new agenda.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The <i>Confounding Legal Text</i>, <i>Confusing Legal Text</i> and <i>Deadly Plot</i> action cards must be played before the hidden agenda is revealed.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;The &lsquo;Legal Text&rsquo; action cards and Deadly Plot must be played before the agenda that was voted on is revealed.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The speaker may still vote on <i>Covert Legislation</i>.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Q: Does the Speaker vote when Covert Legislation is drawn? A: Yes.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the <i>Fleet Regulations</i> law is in play and the <a href="/F_mahact">Mahact</a> player already has four command tokens in their fleet pool, they may add a fifth with their <sc>Edict</sc> faction ability, and then choose one command token to return from their fleet pool to their reinforcements.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If the law Fleet Regulations is in play, and Mahact already has 4 tokens in fleet, can they add another one &hellip;? A: The Mahact player can add a 5th token and choose one to return to their reinforcements from their fleet pool afterward.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A player must still meet the prerequisites for the technology they research.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If an ability instructs you to &lsquo;research&rsquo; a technology, you require the prerequisites on that technology to do so.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>An ability that puts a space dock on the game board by &ldquo;replacing&rdquo;, rather than &ldquo;placing&rdquo;, such as the <i>Infiltrate</i> action card, will trigger <i>Minister of Industry</i>.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Any instance of &lsquo;replace&rsquo; can be considered to say &lsquo;remove and place&rsquo; if no units are left in reinforcements &hellip; Note, this overturns a previous ruling regarding Minister of Industry.&rdquo; Overturns the Oct 3, 2018 ruling (source 5 line 1457).</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If a player controls planets in another player&rsquo;s home system, those planets are not exhausted by the &ldquo;For&rdquo; outcome of <i>New Constitution</i>.<sup>2,3,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Q: Does New Constitution exhaust home planets if they&rsquo;re not controlled by their owner? A: No, you only exhaust planets in your home system if you control them.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If a player wishes to place a mech, but there are none left in their reinforcements, they may remove a mech from any system that does not contain one of their command tokens and place that instead. The mech will be placed undamaged.<sup>1,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If a unit is damaged, and is &lsquo;removed and placed&rsquo; from the board via a game effect, does it come back repaired &hellip;? A: &hellip; If it is produced, placed, or replaced which would require a remove and place it is no longer damaged.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A player with three scored secret objectives may draw a fourth. However, they must immediately shuffle it into the secret objective deck.<sup>1,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling, on drawing past the scored-secret limit: &ldquo;you could draw an additional secret but would then need to return it and shuffle the secret objective deck.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A player must still meet the prerequisites for the technology they research.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If an ability instructs you to &lsquo;research&rsquo; a technology, you require the prerequisites on that technology to do so.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/C_events">Events</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>If multiple players would gain their final victory point simultaneously, the player with the lowest initiative wins.<sup>1,4</sup>
