<h2><a href="/C_relics">Relics</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li>It is public knowledge which action cards a player takes using <i>The Codex</i>.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Are the cards removed from the discard pile via the Relic &lsquo;The Codex&rsquo; public knowledge? A: Yes, the discard is public knowledge.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A player may only reroll combat rolls with <i>The Crown of Thalnos</i>. They cannot reroll anti&ndash;fighter barrage rolls and similar.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;War Funding Omega, War Funding, Munitions Reserves and Crown of Thalnos, are specific to combat rolls.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If a player uses the purge ability of <i>Dynamis Core</i>, they will need to return commodities if they now exceed their original commodity value.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If you have more commodities than your maximum due to purging the Dynamis Core Relic, do you remove commodities to your limit? A: Yes, you discard down.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If a player uses <i>Neuraloop</i> to purge the <i>Dynamis Core</i>, and they have more commodities than their faction&rsquo;s printed commodity value, they return any extras to the supply.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If you have more commodities than your maximum due to purging the Dynamis Core Relic, do you remove commodities to your limit? A: Yes, you discard down.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The <a href="/F_nekro">Nekro</a> player may use the ability of <i>The Prophet&rsquo;s Tears</i> to draw an action card when they would have researched a technology.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Can the Nekro Virus player use the Prophet&rsquo;s Tears Relic? A: Yes, when the Nekro virus player uses their Propagation faction ability, they could exhaust the Relic to gain an action card.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A system that contains a planet destroyed by <i>Stellar Converter</i>, and no other planets, is considered to contain no planets.<sup>2,4,6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;The destroyed planet token is no longer a planet for any purpose, and if it is covering the only planet in a system, that system contains no planets.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2><a href="/C_technology">Technology</a></h2>
<ul>
    <li><i>Sling Relay</i> cannot be used without producing a unit.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Can you Sling Relay without producing anything? A: No, you must produce a ship.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Exhausting planets to gain trade goods can be done at any time during action phase, except when another ability is being resolved. For example, if a player has one of their planets with a technology specialty targeted with the <i>Uprising</i> action card, they cannot use <i>Psychoarchaeology</i> in response to gain a trade good.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling, Nekro agent / Psychoarchaeology / Hacan agent timing: &ldquo;any ability that is used &ldquo;during the action phase&rdquo; cannot be resolved unless there are no other abilities currently being resolved.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If multiple planets are exhausted, the trade goods are gained one at a time.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;When you gain trade goods from multiple planets using the Psychoarchaeology technology, do you gain them 1 at a time or as a group? A: You gain them one at a time.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If a player wishes to place a mech, but there are none left in their reinforcements, they may remove a mech from any system that does not contain one of their command tokens and place that instead. The mech will be placed undamaged.<sup>1,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If a unit is damaged, and is &lsquo;removed and placed&rsquo; from the board via a game effect, does it come back repaired &hellip;? A: &hellip; If it is produced, placed, or replaced which would require a remove and place it is no longer damaged.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Only units participating in the combat may be chosen to be repaired.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Duranium Armor only affects units participating (rolling dice) in a combat.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The ability of <i>Predictive Intelligence</i> to cast additional votes cannot be used if it is exhausted.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Can you cast bonus votes using Predictive Intelligence if the technology is exhausted? A: No, the card being exhausted prevents that ability from being used.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If a mech is damaged when it is removed, it will remain damaged when it is placed.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If it is being removed and placed via an ability such as Transit Diodes it stays in the same state.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
</ul>
